{"type":"message","id":"fb2f0c3f","parentId":"f7671337","timestamp":"2026-06-11T21:53:09.643Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **Market structure & hours:** Stocks trade on regulated exchanges with set market hours and generally stronger investor protections; crypto trades 24/7 on fragmented exchanges with lighter regulation and more platform/custody risk.\n\n- **Volatility & liquidation risk:** Crypto is typically more volatile, so leveraged crypto positions can liquidate faster and from smaller adverse moves; leveraged stocks can still be risky, but price swings are usually less extreme for large-cap equities.\n\n- **Costs, leverage, and transparency:** Stock margin/leverage is often more standardized and broker-regulated, with clearer reporting; crypto leverage can offer much higher multiples, but funding fees, spreads, exchange solvency risk, and sudden liquidity gaps can materially increase risk."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":4215,"output":216,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":4431,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781214782731}}
